Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 15 06:11:05 2026 +1100

    nova: Fail nova_libvirt start without virtlogd
    
    nova_libvirt shares the host's /run, so a virtlogd running on the host
    holds the pidfile and our backgrounded sidecar exits unnoticed. libvirt
    then hands console logs to the host virtlogd, which cannot see instance
    directories, and instance creation fails.
    
    Run virtlogd with --daemon, which returns only once it holds its pidfile
    and socket, so a conflict fails the container at startup. --daemon stops
    virtlogd logging to stderr, so send its log to the kolla log volume.

    Prompt: interactive debugging of an upgrade error report from ``Vii``
    on the #openstack-kolla IRC channel.
    
    Related-Bug: #2155214
    Depends-On: https://review.opendev.org/c/openstack/kolla-ansible/+/1010532
    Change-Id: I31bed46c0ea038886d247bbdc97cc0c8a04b64cc
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context, low effort) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/kolla/docker/nova/nova-libvirt-spice/kolla_nova_libvirt_start.sh b/kolla/docker/nova/nova-libvirt-spice/kolla_nova_libvirt_start.sh
index f06a63d9e..a0e36015d 100644
--- a/kolla/docker/nova/nova-libvirt-spice/kolla_nova_libvirt_start.sh
+++ b/kolla/docker/nova/nova-libvirt-spice/kolla_nova_libvirt_start.sh
@@ -5,8 +5,11 @@ set -euo pipefail
 # nova instance console logs to rotate. Otherwise they will
 # consume unbounded amounts of disk.
 #
-# No exec here: libvirtd will be the "main" process.
-/usr/sbin/virtlogd &
+# virtlogd's pidfile and socket live in the host's /run. --daemon
+# returns only once virtlogd holds both, so a conflicting virtlogd on
+# the host stops the container here instead of being silently used.
+LIBVIRT_LOG_OUTPUTS="3:file:/var/log/kolla/libvirt/virtlogd.log" \
+    /usr/sbin/virtlogd --daemon
 
 # Now hand over PID 1's direct child role to libvirtd.
 exec /usr/sbin/libvirtd --listen
